# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Secp256k1 recoverable signing for Tron"
description: """
Signs the 32-byte SHA-256 digest of a serialized raw_data and produces Tron's
65-byte r-s-v wire signature, where v is the raw recovery id.

Secret-dependent curve operations use mirage-crypto-ec's fiat-crypto P256k1
backend. Recovery, which runs on public data, uses mirage-crypto-blockchain's
reference implementation -- which is documented NOT CONSTANT TIME and must
never be handed a secret key. This split follows ocaml-evm's evm-crypto.

No RNG: nonces are RFC 6979 deterministic."""
